Spoilers...

The Gnome Mines can get pretty tough down low, especially if you're weak
and have no light source.

The only thing I can see that's good about the Gnome Mines is (A) The
town, and (B) The Luckstone.  There's a luckstone down there somewhere,
you just gotta find it.

Another difficulty is being neutral.  Sometimes a peaceful Gnome will
pick up the luckstone and you can't kill him for it.  Not without making
your God angry, anyway.

A couple solutions to this are: Have a strong pet, who can easily dispatch
Gnomes and Dwarves.  Or find one of those falling-rock traps and lure the
bastards into it.

Be careful.  I've found plenty of loadstones down there too.  A good test
is to try kicking the gray stone before you pick it up.  If it goes
*THUMP*, leave it alone.


